Architecture plan for issues #208-#210

Goal
- Apply a small brand/content refresh to the existing Rust Axum + Askama server-rendered blog without changing routing, data models, storage behavior, or deployment shape.
- Keep visual brand assets and text/SEO copy consistent across the header, footer, favicon, homepage, and template tests.

Current relevant structure
- `public/images/`
  - `ideavibes-wordmark.svg`: source logo used by the shared header/footer templates.
  - `ideavibes-mark.svg`: standalone brand mark asset.
- `public/favicon.ico`
  - Browser favicon currently served by Axum through `ServeFile` at `/favicon.ico`.
- `rust-backend/templates/layout.html`
  - Shared HTML shell and favicon/link metadata location if `favicon.svg` is added.
- `rust-backend/templates/partials/header.html`
  - Shared top navigation logo image reference.
- `rust-backend/templates/partials/footer.html`
  - Shared footer logo image reference and tagline copy.
- `rust-backend/templates/public/home.html`
  - Homepage sections, including the intro block targeted by #209.
- `rust-backend/src/main.rs`
  - Public route handlers and homepage context strings passed into Askama templates.
- `rust-backend/src/html/seo.rs`
  - Default site description/SEO fallback copy.
- `rust-backend/src/html/mod.rs`
  - Rendering tests/fixtures that assert shared layout and homepage/footer copy.

Issue dependency order
1. #208 Use the Ideavibes logo image and a sail-only favicon
   - Update static brand assets first because header/footer references already point at the shared SVG path.
   - Regenerate `public/favicon.ico` from the sail-only mark; optionally add `public/favicon.svg` and link it from `layout.html`.
   - Verify header/footer still reference the correct wordmark path and dimensions/alt text remain appropriate.
2. #209 Remove the homepage intro block
   - Remove the hero intro markup from `home.html`.
   - Clear or stop populating the corresponding `heading` and `intro` strings in `main.rs` for consistency with the template.
   - Update rendering tests in `html/mod.rs` so they no longer expect the removed intro copy.
3. #210 Change the tagline to "From idea to product."
   - Change the footer copy in `partials/footer.html`.
   - Update `DEFAULT_DESCRIPTION` in `html/seo.rs` to the same sentence so visible copy and metadata stay aligned.
   - Adjust any tests/fixtures asserting the previous tagline.

Shared design decisions
- Keep the product/brand name exactly as provided by the issues: Ideavibes / ideavibes. Do not introduce agent/platform placeholder names.
- Prefer static asset replacement over template rewiring: keep `/images/ideavibes-wordmark.svg` and `/images/ideavibes-mark.svg` stable unless the issue explicitly requires an additional favicon link.
- The favicon mark should be sail-only: no wordmark, no red dot, no background. The full wordmark remains only in `ideavibes-wordmark.svg` for header/footer use.
- Keep Askama contexts small and compatible. If `heading`/`intro` become unused after #209, remove them from homepage context structs only if tests and handlers can be updated in that issue without broad churn; otherwise clear the strings and leave structural cleanup for the same issue.
- Preserve Axum static serving and proxy-aware deployment behavior; these issues should not alter route topology, database access, auth, object storage, newsletter flows, or admin forms.
- Run the existing validation for each implementation session: CSS build, Rust backend build/tests, and targeted rendered-HTML assertions.
